## Comprehensive Report: EmptyViewHandler and Swipe-to-Remove + Undo Snackbar Logic

Based on my thorough exploration of the AntennaPod project, here are my findings:

### 1. EmptyViewHandler Class

**Finding:** There is **NO separate EmptyViewHandler class** in this codebase. Empty view handling is implemented directly in the fragment classes using manual visibility management of a TextView with id `android:empty`.

**Empty View Implementation Pattern:**
- Empty views are simple TextViews with id `@id/android:empty` defined in XML layouts
- Visibility is toggled manually in fragments using `setVisibility(View.VISIBLE/View.GONE)`
- No custom handler class or adapter observer pattern is used

---

### 2. QueueFragment - Swipe-to-Remove + Undo Implementation

**File:** `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-1130/app/src/main/java/de/danoeh/antennapod/fragment/QueueFragment.java`

#### Empty View Management (Lines 497-500, 513-519, 630-632):
```java
// Initialization in onCreateView
txtvEmpty = root.findViewById(android.R.id.empty);
txtvEmpty.setVisibility(View.GONE);
progLoading = root.findViewById(R.id.progLoading);
progLoading.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);

// In onFragmentLoaded()
if(queue == null || queue.size() == 0) {
    recyclerView.setVisibility(View.GONE);
    txtvEmpty.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
} else {
    txtvEmpty.setVisibility(View.GONE);
    recyclerView.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
}
```

#### Swipe-to-Remove Implementation (Lines 395-494):
- ItemTouchHelper.SimpleCallback attached in onCreateView (line 495):
```java
itemTouchHelper.attachToRecyclerView(recyclerView);
```

- onSwiped() callback (lines 425-443):
```java
@Override
public void onSwiped(RecyclerView.ViewHolder viewHolder, int direction) {
    if(subscription != null) {
        subscription.unsubscribe();
    }
    final int position = viewHolder.getAdapterPosition();
    Log.d(TAG, "remove(" + position + ")");
    final FeedItem item = queue.get(position);
    final boolean isRead = item.isPlayed();
    DBWriter.markItemPlayed(FeedItem.PLAYED, false, item.getId());
    DBWriter.removeQueueItem(getActivity(), item, true);

    Snackbar snackbar = Snackbar.make(root, getString(R.string.marked_as_read_label), Snackbar.LENGTH_LONG);
    snackbar.setAction(getString(R.string.undo), v -> {
        DBWriter.addQueueItemAt(getActivity(), item.getId(), position, false);
        if(!isRead) {
            DBWriter.markItemPlayed(FeedItem.UNPLAYED, item.getId());
        }
    });
    snackbar.show();
}
```

#### RecyclerView Adapter Data Observer Logic:
- Uses ItemTouchHelperViewHolder interface callbacks in QueueRecyclerAdapter (lines 326-342):
```java
public interface ItemTouchHelperViewHolder {
    void onItemSelected();   // Called when swiping starts
    void onItemClear();      // Called when swiping ends
}
```

- ViewHolder implementations (lines 196-203 in QueueRecyclerAdapter.java):
```java
@Override
public void onItemSelected() {
    itemView.setAlpha(0.5f);
}

@Override
public void onItemClear() {
    itemView.setAlpha(1.0f);
}
```

